/-!
# Natural-plus-dual model geometry

The actual automorphism extension is constructed, its layer is identified with
the inner subgroup, and compatible group and linear comparisons are constructed
from a natural layer module and its complementary outer image. The coordinate
and marked developments prove quadratic-form uniqueness and the exact three
nonzero-vector orbits, including inner transitivity on pairing-one vectors.
The standard Sylow fixed-line calculations discharge the existential Sylow
characterization of the singular diagonal orbit.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, H.9.1(1–2), printed pp.389–390.
-/
